<task id="033" project="spaarkeai-compose-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>G5 — Hyperlink support on both paths (authored w:hyperlink render + edit hyperlink op)</title>
    <phase>3 Concurrency + UX</phase>
    <gate>dep:004</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Touches the BFF byte-authors (ComposeDocumentRenderer clean path + ComposeShadowPatchEngine tracked path), extends the closed op catalog with a new hyperlink op + `link` ComposeMarkType, and re-enables a guarded control. High blast radius across renderer + op catalog + engine; a silent-loss round-trip is a data-loss path (NFR-08). Code-review + adr-check run at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Extends the frozen/closed ComposeOperation catalog (ADR-039) and both byte-authors with a new op + mark + engine applier; architectural / high-blast-radius work with OOXML representability judgment (w:hyperlink relationship handling).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>shared renderer (ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs) + op catalog (ComposeOperation.cs ↔ compose-operations.ts) + engine (ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs) + toolbar (ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx). Overlaps other op-catalog/engine tasks. Run /conflict-check before every BFF PR (overlaps compose-r1/r2/r3 + ai-architecture-redesign-r2 + analysis-hub-r1 shared client).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>004</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, compose, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>M-L (3-6d)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement hyperlink support on BOTH Compose paths (spec FR-05 / gap G5 / SDL-4/5). AUTHORED path: add `href` to ComposeInlineRun and emit `w:hyperlink` in ComposeDocumentRenderer.BuildRun (:366) / AssembleParagraph (:346). EDIT path: add a hyperlink op to the closed catalog + `link` to ComposeMarkType + an engine applier in ComposeShadowPatchEngine. Re-enable the hyperlink control (ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx :635, disabled in BOTH modes today). Add seam slices on BOTH paths (authored → clean w:hyperlink; imported → tracked). Extend the closed catalog — never fork (ADR-039). If a hyperlink round-trips as unrepresentable / silent-loss, STOP.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with OOXML/DocumentFormat.OpenXml expertise (w:hyperlink + relationship handling), Compose Shadow Document engine familiarity (ADR-049), and React/Fluent v9 toolbar experience.</role>

  <goal>A hyperlink survives BOTH paths: (1) AUTHORED — `href` on ComposeInlineRun renders as a clean `w:hyperlink` via ComposeDocumentRenderer.BuildRun/AssembleParagraph (zero tracked markup); (2) EDIT — a new hyperlink op in the closed ComposeOperation catalog (mirrored in compose-operations.ts) + `link` in ComposeMarkType + a ComposeShadowPatchEngine applier that emits a tracked hyperlink on imported docs; (3) the hyperlink control (ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx :635) is re-enabled in both modes; (4) seam slices prove both paths round-trip with untouched subtrees byte-identical and no unrepresentable/silent-loss path. SDL-4/5 guards removed.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec FR-05 (G5 / SDL-4/5) and plan P3-4, R4 guarded hyperlinks: the control is disabled in BOTH modes (ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx :635) and hyperlinks are unrepresentable, so they were silently lost. R5 removes the guard by building the feature: the authored renderer emits clean `w:hyperlink`, and the edit path adds a hyperlink op + `link` mark + engine applier for tracked hyperlinks on imported docs. Each gap's exit criterion is removing its R4 guard with a seam slice proving the construct round-trips and the no-error / no-silent-loss invariant holds.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/Operations/ComposeOperation.cs</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-operations.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx</file>
      <file>tests/integration/seam/Compose/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>Task 004 (op-schema extension design — the shape the closed catalog extends with). Extend, never fork.</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Honor I-1…I-7 + D1–D5. Engine is byte[]-in/byte[]-out; the edit applier is a surgical op anchored by (paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset); untouched OOXML subtrees stay byte-identical after save. Preserve the two-byte-author split (renderer clean / engine tracked) — do not merge the authors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">I-7 / NFR-02: NO text-search anywhere in the write path — resolve the hyperlink target run by (paraId, runIndex, offset), never content match.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Closed op catalog: the new hyperlink op EXTENDS the catalog under version control (server ComposeOperation.cs `[JsonDerivedType]` :148-157 ↔ client compose-operations.ts :54-64) — never fork, no side channel, no new AI dispatch endpoint. AI redline path stays envelope-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI internals in Services/Compose/ (Tier-1 NetArchTest). No IOpenAiClient/executor/routing types in the renderer or engine.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Patch engine = stateless concrete singleton; the new hyperlink applier carries no per-request state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">No Microsoft.Graph above SpeFileStore; hyperlink relationship handling stays in the OOXML byte-authors, not a Graph call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Seam DoD: BOTH paths carry through-the-wire WebApplicationFactory seam slices in tests/integration/seam/Compose/ (authored clean w:hyperlink; imported tracked). NO Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-01: corpus byte-diff harness (24/24) MUST NOT regress. NFR-08: removing the SDL-4/5 guard MUST NOT reintroduce a user-triggerable error or silent-loss path; the R4 op-log-preservation net stays until this feature is seam-proven.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-03/04: MIT/permissive only; NO new runtime package (DocumentFormat.OpenXml already present). Report absolute BFF publish size + delta vs ~46.11 MB baseline; ≤60 MB compressed ceiling.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-09 (analysis-hub-r1): shared Spaarke.Compose.Components surface + save/redline contract MUST NOT regress the downstream consumer's reopen-restore parity. Run /conflict-check before the BFF + shared-client PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF task — state Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). All new hyperlink surface lands in Services/Compose/ (renderer + engine); no new service, library, or endpoint family.</constraint>
  </constraints>

