  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbors: ComposeMarkType enum (ComposeOperation.cs:101) for marks; ComposeDocumentRenderer.BuildRun:366 for run authoring; the closed op catalog `[JsonDerivedType]` set (ComposeOperation.cs:148-157). Grep confirms no existing hyperlink op and no `link`/`href` in ComposeMarkType or ComposeInlineRun today (the control at ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx:635 is disabled precisely because hyperlinks are unrepresentable).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — EXTEND, not fork. `link` is added to the existing ComposeMarkType enum; `href` is added to the existing ComposeInlineRun; the hyperlink op is added to the existing closed ComposeOperation catalog under version control (ADR-039 R5-D3). The applier is a new branch alongside ApplyInsertText/WrapRunAsDeleted, not a new engine. No new service, class family, or endpoint.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Concrete failure: a user who inserts a hyperlink today has it silently dropped (unrepresentable) and the hyperlink control stays disabled in both modes — authored docs cannot carry a link, and imported-doc hyperlink edits are lost with no error. FR-05 / SDL-4/5 acceptance cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the op-schema extension design from task 004 and confirm the hyperlink op shape. Read ComposeMarkType (:101), ComposeInlineRun, ComposeDocumentRenderer.BuildRun (:366)/AssembleParagraph (:346), and the tracked appliers (ApplyInsertText:314 / WrapRunAsDeleted:942).</step>
    <step order="2">AUTHORED path: add `href` to ComposeInlineRun; emit clean `w:hyperlink` in ComposeDocumentRenderer.BuildRun/AssembleParagraph (handle the OOXML hyperlink relationship correctly; zero text-search — the cited I-5 clean-author exception). Untouched subtrees stay byte-identical.</step>
    <step order="3">EDIT path: extend the closed catalog with the hyperlink op (ComposeOperation.cs :148-157) + `link` in ComposeMarkType (:101); mirror both in client compose-operations.ts (:54-64). Emit the hyperlink op from classifyStep (stepOperationInterceptor.ts :442, today unrepresentable/defer). Add a ComposeShadowPatchEngine applier that emits a tracked hyperlink on imported docs, surgical and (paraId,runIndex,offset)-anchored — never content match (NFR-02).</step>
    <step order="4">Re-enable the hyperlink control in ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx (:635) for BOTH modes. Anchor the control's UI to the existing toolbar styling.</step>
    <step order="5">Add seam slices in tests/integration/seam/Compose/ for BOTH paths: authored → clean w:hyperlink (no tracked markup); imported → tracked hyperlink; both prove untouched subtrees byte-identical and no unrepresentable/silent-loss. Add the &lt;ui-tests&gt; below.</step>
    <step order="6">Run /conflict-check before opening the BFF + shared-client PR (renderer/engine/op-catalog overlap with compose-r1/r2/r3 + ai-architecture-redesign-r2; toolbar overlap with analysis-hub-r1). State Placement Justification and report publish-size delta vs ~46.11 MB in the PR.</step>
    <step order="7">Run/verify: build (BFF + Spaarke.Compose.Components) + both seam slices + ui-tests + corpus byte-diff (24/24) + Tier-1 NetArchTest pass.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r5/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a hyperlink round-trips as unrepresentable or silent-loss on either path (i.e., the authored w:hyperlink or the tracked edit applier cannot faithfully preserve the link target/text through save+reload), STOP and escalate — this is a data-loss path (NFR-08). Do not re-enable the control while a silent-loss path remains.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF, run both seam slices + Tier-1 NetArchTest, run dotnet publish for the size delta.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build Spaarke.Compose.Components and run the client/ui tests.</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run /conflict-check on the BFF + shared-client surface.</tool>
  </tools>

