  </outputs>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="insert-hyperlink-authored">Given an authored (born-in-editor) doc, when the user inserts a hyperlink and saves, then the link renders and the saved OOXML carries a clean w:hyperlink (no tracked markup).</test>
    <test name="insert-hyperlink-imported">Given an imported doc, when the user inserts a hyperlink, then the edit is captured as the hyperlink op and applies as a tracked hyperlink.</test>
    <test name="control-enabled-both-modes">Given the toolbar, when a doc is loaded in either mode, then the hyperlink control (ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx :635) is re-enabled (no longer disabled), anchored to existing toolbar styling.</test>
    <test name="dark-mode">Given ADR-021 dark mode, when the hyperlink control and rendered links display in dark theme, then they use theme tokens (no hard-coded colors) and remain legible in both light and dark.</test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an authored doc with an href on a ComposeInlineRun, when it saves, then ComposeDocumentRenderer emits a clean w:hyperlink and the corpus byte-diff shows untouched subtrees byte-identical (SDL-4 guard removed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an imported doc, when the user inserts a hyperlink, then the new hyperlink op (extended into the closed catalog, mirrored client+server) applies as a tracked hyperlink via ComposeShadowPatchEngine, anchored by (paraId,runIndex,offset) with no text-search (SDL-5 guard removed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given both paths, when the seam slices run through the WebApplicationFactory, then authored (clean) and imported (tracked) hyperlinks round-trip with no unrepresentable/silent-loss and no banned mock/DI/ctor test shapes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the toolbar, when a doc is loaded, then the hyperlink control is enabled in both modes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative / no-regression: op catalog is EXTENDED not forked (ADR-039); Tier-1 NetArchTest passes (no AI internals); corpus byte-diff stays 24/24; BFF publish ≤60 MB (delta vs ~46.11 MB reported); no new runtime package; the two-byte-author split is preserved; analysis-hub-r1 reopen-restore parity not regressed (NFR-09).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-05 / gap G5 / SDL-4/5; plan P3-4. Both paths (authored render + edit op). NEW hyperlink op + `link` mark → justification emitted. Deps 004 (op-schema design). parallel-safe=false due to shared renderer + op catalog + engine + toolbar. Escalate on any unrepresentable/silent-loss round-trip (NFR-08).</notes>

